513, 0.03034159354865551, -0.015715528279542923, 0.010908265598118305, -0.014190278016030788, 0.011303196661174297, 0.046193305402994156, -0.016042368486523628, 0.00880423653870821, 0.03159447759389877, -0.02014147862792015, 0.0038063174579292536, 0.006993001792579889, -0.0006502742762677372, 0.002553432947024703, 0.002938150195404887, 0.010894647799432278, -0.008143749088048935], "index": 8, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7649, "total_tokens": 7649}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 3631 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Vertical Layout in the Process Editor\nDescription: The vertical layout is now generally available.  These are some of the advantages that the new layout offers you:      To move process steps that have already been connected to the process, you simply select the step and drag and drop it.      You can access embedded help using the question mark button (?). In the Help Panel, you can navigate between the help for UI elements, the embedded What's New, and the Guided Tours.      If, for example, the outcome of an approval step in your process is “reject”, you can insert a go-to step and send users back to a previous step asking them to rework their entries.  See Use Cases for Custom Variables.      The side panel is wider and easier to work with. You can close it to save space. To display process information again, use the toggle button in the side panel.      You can select the next step to insert in your process from the smart menu.  See step 6 in Create a Business Process.      Steps with more than one flow are visualized as a group. You can collapse groups to get a better overview of the whole process.      The process is always valid, there are no more dangling ends. If you add a new step, for example, an approval form, all output paths are connected. You do not have to connect, for example, the Reject outcome to the process anymore.      See Create and Configure Forms in a Vertical Layout Process Editor.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-01-22\nValid as Of: 2024-01-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3632 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Administrative Data in the Documentation Template\nDescription: You can now select whether you want to display the administrative data of your MIG and MAG in the documentation template.  See: MIGs and MAGs\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3633 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Display xsd:nillable value in a MIG\nDescription: You can now view if an element/node in a MIG allows nil values through the Nillable field.  See: Working with a Node\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3634 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 1.82.*    Increment: 2312    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3635 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Support of xsd:nillable in Custom Messages\nDescription: Custom Messages now support xsd:nillable.  See: Custom Type Systems\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3636 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.23.*    Increment: 2312  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3637 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Add System Version for SAP Process Orchestration Systems\nDescription: When adding a new SAP Process Orchestration System, you can now select the system version, or have the application auto-detect it.  See Add an SAP Process Orchestration System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3638 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Rules Added\nDescription: The following rules have been added for Migration Assessment:      SenderMailPostprocessing: Evaluate the postprocessing steps (Delete, Mark as Read, Archive) of the mail sender adapter.      SenderMailTransportProtocol: Evaluate the mail protocol.      SenderRESTErrorHandling: Evaluate the error handling of the sender REST adapter.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3639 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Migration Assessment: 1.23.*      Increment: 2312    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision", " New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3639 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Migration Assessment: 1.23.*      Increment: 2312    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3640 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create an Agreement\nDescription: With alias based configuration of agreement templates, you can now choose to copy or reference the B2B Scenarios while creating an agreement.  See: Trading Partner Agreement  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n", "--- Record 2961 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Global References for API Artifact\nDescription: In addition to including local resources within your API artifact, such as database connections or configuration files, you can also make use of reusable message mappings, which allow you to define standardized mappings between different message formats. Script collections, on the other hand, provide a library of pre-built scripts that can be easily reused across multiple API endpoints. Message type libraries and function libraries offer a centralized repository of message types and functions that can be shared and utilized throughout your API development process.  See: Manage Resources\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: 2403\n\n--- Record 2962 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Message Service (Solace Broker) alerts\nDescription: You can now subscribe for Message Service (Solace Broker) alerts.  See: Alerting\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: 2403\n\n--- Record 2963 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Rollback\nDescription: You can now rollback the deployment of the Edge Integration Cell solution to its last successful version if an upgrade or configuration modification operation fails.  See: Rollback Edge Integration Cell Solution\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: 2403\n\n--- Record 2964 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Edge Integration Cell: 8.16.*      Increment: 2403    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: 2403\n\n--- Record 2965 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Better Extraction of rawValue for Standard Document Types and Fields\nDescription: The extraction of the rawValue response field has been improved for the standard document types and fields.  See Get Result.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2966 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Better Models for the Extraction of Standard Document Types\nDescription: The machine learning models for the extraction of invoice, paymentAdvice, and purchaseOrder documents have been improved.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2967 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UI5 Version Upgrade for Reuse UI\nDescription: The UI5 version for the Reuse UI component is now updated to 1.120.12  See Reuse UI.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-10\nValid as Of: 2024-05-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2968 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.27.*      Increment: 2403    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-10\nValid as Of: 2024-05-10\nVersion: 2403\n\n--- Record 2969 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.6.1\nDescription: The release 1.6.1 of the Istio module includes the following changes:        We’ve updated Istio to version 1.21.1. For more information, see Istio 1.21.1 Release Announcement and Change Notes.    Now, you can configure externalTrafficPolicy for Istio Ingress Gateway and use the X-Forwarded-For (XFF) header in all cloud service providers. See Forward the Client IP in the XFF Header.    We’ve fixed cluster provider discovery by implementing node-based discovery.      \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-10\nValid as Of: 2024-05-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2970 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Migration Assessment: 1.27.*      Increment: 2403    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-10\nValid as Of: 2024-05-10\nVersion: 2403\n\n", "--- Record 1401 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Develop Custom Actions with the IDE Action Framework and Enhance Them with Server-Driven UI\nDescription: The IDE Action framework allows you to extend the ABAP development tools for Eclipse with custom actions. You can create and run IDE Actions, which are additional functionalities implemented completely in the backend. On top of that, you have the option to use server-driven UI APIs to build UIs, add parameters and additional configurations to your actions, such as side effects and custom value helps.  See IDE Actions and Working with Server-Driven UIs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1402 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Update Accessible Resources in Cloud Connector\nDescription: The accessible resources for the Custom Code Migration app have been extended with function module RS_ABAP_INFRA_VERSION_E. The accessible resources need to be updated in the Cloud Connector after the upgrade.  See 2861842 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1403 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Updated ATC Check \"Allowed Object Types in Cloud\"\nDescription: The ATC check \"Allowed Object Types in Cloud\" now only reports findings if the ABAP language version of the object is set to \"Standard\". It no longer reports findings for objects that have already been specified for usage in cloud and their ABAP language version has been set to \"ABAP Cloud Development\" or \"Key User\".\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1404 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Working with Intelligent Scenarios and Intelligent Scenario Models\nDescription: You can now work with Intelligent Scenarios and Intelligent Scenario Models in ABAP development tools for Eclipse in addition to the corresponding apps on the Fiori launchpad.  SeeWorking with Intelligent Scenarios and Working with Intelligent Scenario Models.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1405 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP SQL Service - (read-only) Database Procedures\nDescription: Have you already used the ABAP SQL Service / ODBC Driver for ABAP to expose ABAP-based business data via SQL-APIs to external SQL consumers? We are now increasing the feature scope for those scenarios. Besides exposing CDS view entities for read-only scenarios, it will be possible to also expose \"read-only\" AMDP-based database procedures to be used by external ODBC clients. By doing so, you can both expose SQL and SQLScript-based business logic to external ODBC clients.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1406 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: CDS Table Entities\nDescription: A new type of CDS entity is available: the CDS table entity. A CDS table entity defines a database table in ABAP CDS as an ABAP-managed database object. Table entities provide a persistence layer for ABAP applications that allows you to define and manage SAP HANA database tables as native CDS repository objects. The initial shipment of table entities supports CDS associations, CDS annotations, and typing with both CDS simple types and CDS enumerated types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1407 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: CDS Updatable View Entities\nDescription: With CDS Writeable View Entities, you can wrap existing DDIC Tables (or CDS Table Entities) and expose a native CDS signature that you can use with ABAP SQL (SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) in combination with DCL-based access control. CDS Writeable View Entities are projections based on the underlying DDIC Table / CDS Table Entity.  CDS Writeable View Entities will allow the following scenarios:  Enabling of \"Cloud-ready\" READ/WRITE AMDPs, as they ensure \"client safe\" native HANA SQLScript coding by preventing cross-client access  Exposure of a stable CDS signature for full SQL DML access but still allowing changes to the underlying persistence model  Enabling the usage of Dynamic View Caches based on released SAP content  Enabling of WRITE scenarios via the ABAP SQL Service / ABAP ODBC Driver  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest", "RITE AMDPs, as they ensure \"client safe\" native HANA SQLScript coding by preventing cross-client access  Exposure of a stable CDS signature for full SQL DML access but still allowing changes to the underlying persistence model  Enabling the usage of Dynamic View Caches based on released SAP content  Enabling of WRITE scenarios via the ABAP SQL Service / ABAP ODBC Driver  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1408 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Changing the HTTP Redirect Behavior\nDescription: You can now change and the redirect behavior or retrieve the current redirect policy of an HTTP call using the SET_REDIRECT_POLICY and GET_REDIRECT_POLICY methods of the CL_WEB_HTTP_CLIENT_MANAGER class.  For more information, see Changing the HTTP Redirect Behavior.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1409 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Cipher Suites\nDescription: You can now specify cipher suites in the Communication Systems app to define a set of encryption mechanisms you want to use as a basis for your communication.  See How to Create Communication Systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1410 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Client Safety of CDS and AMDP\nDescription: To support client safe implementation please read Client Handling in ABAP - SAP Community for an overview.  Technical background is provided in 3472859 .  Please adopt these recommendations. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3641 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Migrate an Agreement\nDescription: With the introduction of Creation Mode in agreements, you need to migrate your old agreements to the new format to continue editing/copying.  See: Migrating an Agreement\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3642 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 6.44.*  Increment: 2312  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3643 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Build API Actions from Scratch\nDescription: We have introduced a new option called Build from Scratch, which allows you to easily create API actions from scratch, providing a more flexible and customized experience.  For more information about creating a custom action project, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-19\nValid as Of: 2024-01-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3644 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Consume API Actions using API Business Hub Enterprise\nDescription: Your business processes can consume APIs managed by your organization. To consume such APIs, create an action project using API Business Hub Enterprise.  For more information about creating an action project, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-19\nValid as Of: 2024-01-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3645 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Domain Changes\nDescription: In March 2024, the domain for SAP Build Process Automation will change. If you are using a firewall, you must adapt your firewall rules to allow access to the tenant. If you want to use debug mode with agent versions below 3.13.52 and below 2.0.35, you must update the tenant domain in the agent.  See 3440715 .\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-18\nValid as Of: 2024-01-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3646 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: New Machine Type in the Microsoft Azure and Azure Lite plans\nDescription: A new Machine Type, Dsv5-series, has been added to the Microsoft Azure and Azure Lite plans. It supports online volume resizing without any downtime. You can migrate to the new type by updating the Machine Type parameter.  For more information, go to the Machine Type parameter's detailed specification.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-16\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3647 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Supported versions for Cloud Build Service\nDescription: We've updated the supported versions for the Cloud Build service:    January 2024    Mobile Development Kit SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      SAP Asset Manager Android and iOS versions, and notes          December 2023    Mobile Development Kit SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      SAP Asset Manager SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes          November 2023 - Mobile Development Kit SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      See Supported Build Types, Client Types, Packaging Details, and Build Options. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3648 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Supported versions for Cloud Build Service\nDescription: We've updated the supported versions for the Cloud Build service:    January 2024 (2305 PL11) Mobile Development Kit SDK version, iOS version, and notes      December 2023 (2305 PL09)    Fiori Packaged SDK version, UI5 version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      Custom Fiori Client SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      Mobile Development Kit SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes      SAP Asset Manager SDK version, Android and iOS versions, and notes          November 2023 (2305 PL08) Mobile Development Kit SDK version and notes      See Supported Build Types, Client Types, Packaging Details, and Build Options. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3649 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extension Concept - Proper Display of HANA DECIMAL-Type Columns in Local Extension Database Access\nDescription: Reading call values from DECIMAL type columns in the local extension database access used to display unprocessable result. This issue has", "Type: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3649 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extension Concept - Proper Display of HANA DECIMAL-Type Columns in Local Extension Database Access\nDescription: Reading call values from DECIMAL type columns in the local extension database access used to display unprocessable result. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-16\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3650 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2024.2\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data cataloging, data integration, and data modeling.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2024.2. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1371 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.24.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.23.0 to 2.24.0. Updated components:      Apache TomEE 10 is now added to the buildpack.      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.23.7 to 2.23.8      SapMachine 17 is updated from version 17.0.13 to 17.0.14      SapMachine 21 is updated from version 21.0.5 to 21.0.6      PostgreSQL JDBC Driver (postgresql.version) is updated from 42.7.4 to 42.7.5      SAP BTP Environment Variable Access (com.sap.cloud.environment.servicebinding) is updated from version 0.10.5 to 0.20.0       otel-agent is updated from version 2.10.0 to 2.11.0      otel-agent-ext-java is updated from version 1.5.21 to 1.5.22      logback is updated from version 1.5.15 to 1.5.16      logback-access is updated from version 2.0.5 to 2.0.6      com.sap.xs.onpremise.runtime is updated from version 1.3.0 to 1.3.3      com.sap.core.connectivity.jco is updated from version 3.4.8 to 3.4.9      org.apache.httpcomponents.client5.httpclient5 is updated from version 5.3.1 to 5.4.1      org.json is updated from version 20240303 to 20250107      com.sap.cloud.security.xsuaa is updated from version 3.5.4 to 3.5.7    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-05\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1372 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automatic Theme Detection\nDescription: It is now possible to automatically detect the theme of the operating system and display SAP Start with the corresponding theme.  To enable this, a new option, Automatic (based on your operating system settings), was added to: Settings  Appearance  Theme.  The automatic theme detection is available for all theme sets (such as the SAP Quartz and the SAP Horizon sets) where there is more than one theme available in the set.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1373 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Themes Are Arranged in Categories\nDescription: The themes under Settings  Appearance  Theme are now arranged according to the following categories:    SAP Quartz (Set)  SAP Horizon (Set)  Individual Themes  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1374 ---\nComponent: SAPUI5\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: SAPUI5 Distribution 1.133\nDescription: SAPUI5 version 1.133 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. It’s up to the services to determine when they start using the new version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1375 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.14.1\nDescription: Restarting sidecars is now divided into two phases. In the first phase, only Kyma workloads are restarted. If this phase fails, the Istio Custom Resource (CR) is set to the Error state. In the second phase, customer workloads are restarted in chunks. If any iteration of this phase fails, the Istio CR is set to the Warning state.  We have increased global metrics rotation interval to 6 hours.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-12\nValid as Of: 2025-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1376 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: New subaccount and cluster regions available for the Kyma environment\nDescription:     Canada (Toronto) (cf-ca20) running on Microsoft Azure is now available as a new subaccount region for use with enterprise accounts and Partner Test, Demo, and Development accounts (azure_lite).  Japan (Tokyo) (cf-jp31) and KSA (Dammam) (cf-sa31) running on Google Cloud are now available as new subaccount regions for use with enterprise accounts.  Canada (Toronto) (canadacentral) running on Microsoft Azure is now available as a new cluster region.  Japan (Tokyo) (asia-northeast1), Singapore (Jurong West) (asia-southeast1),", " Development accounts (azure_lite).  Japan (Tokyo) (cf-jp31) and KSA (Dammam) (cf-sa31) running on Google Cloud are now available as new subaccount regions for use with enterprise accounts.  Canada (Toronto) (canadacentral) running on Microsoft Azure is now available as a new cluster region.  Japan (Tokyo) (asia-northeast1), Singapore (Jurong West) (asia-southeast1), North America (Oregon) (us-west1), North America (Virginia) (us-east4), and Europe (Netherlands) (europe-west4) running on Google Cloud are now available as new cluster regions.      For more information, see Regions for the Kyma Environment and Provisioning and Updating Parameters in the Kyma Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-19\nValid as Of: 2025-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1377 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.33.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:  All telemetry data is now enriched with cloud provider specific resource attributes like the region and zone of the related workloads (#1685).  Metrics/Traces: Update to OTel Collector 0.118.0 (#1787).  Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 3.2.4 (#1781).  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-05\nValid as Of: 2025-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1378 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Best Practices - Embedded Web Pages in SAP WinGUI\nDescription: You can now manually capture screens with embedded web pages and automate them.See Guidelines for the SAP GUI Technology Automation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-19\nValid as Of: 2025-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1379 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Known Issues - Managing data type changes in process variables\nDescription: When you change the data type of a Process Variable, you might encounter some challenges.See Known Issues.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-19\nValid as Of: 2025-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1380 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.4\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data integration and data modeling.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.4. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-19\nValid as Of: 2025-02-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_71ebc3a006140a22b4998335e6bad49a390f2cff55f44e185fea0b835edb259a_v2"}